Ascension #3
Kryslon-sam-hum-fem-law

Wanted to try something different, more combat oriented. Didn't cast a
spell (intentionally .. I tried to cast jump to confuse myself a few
times).

The survival of this one was in doubt for a while. I encountered a
Master Lich in Mine's end who successfully evaporated my starting
splint mail and some gloves. I did not finish Mine's end until late (I
think I had visited the castle already), but I needed that luckstone
because I wasn't getting Grayswandir.

And I nearly died the level above fighting a vampire. Thankfully, I
had a wand of fire and zapped Elbereth.

I nearly died again on that level being hugged by an owlbear. That
wand of fire saved my butt again.

Finally, my last real brush with death happened when I found a throne
room with a Black Dragon ... it was out of melee range so its
disintegration blast took out some more armor (but thankfully did not
disintegrate me!!) ... it also bounced back and whizzed by me, the RNG
+ luck saved my hide.

Soon after I polypiled some amulets and came up with an amulet of
reflection. My confidence in the character's ascendability increased
significantly. But I knew Liches and Nagas and Rodney could still
destroy my armor ... I used the WoW for charging (it was 0:1), then
GDSM, a couple magic markers for making ?oEA and ?oEW, and its final
wish for a charging scroll for the magic marker.

I genocided L, ;, and h. A couple throne genocides and cockatrices
were gone (new moon) as well as disenchanters (twice they took my
katana from +7 to +4.

Elemental planes were boring again. I didn't realize crystal balls
needed intelligence because it fizzled on me in the plane of water. I
tried to use the AoY to guide me but it was pretty useless. I wasted
quite a few turns wandering around. Some nice person watching me sent
me some mail, reminding me it could be hiding under an item (thanks,
whoever it was!).

Astal plane was easy with conflict. As magicians I never bothered with
the priest(esse)s and Angels but I thought I'd take a few out for fun.
It was a 2-altar trip, I never saw Death. A total of 2656 turns from
grabbing the amulet to ascension (59511 to 62167). Fun fun.

